       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for extended-release is 2,000 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose.** If you want 1,700 mg three times daily as written, please confirm it's intentional, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nOnce you tell me which, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
